Subject: [PATCH v2 0/7] Add just process-email
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev

This adds `just process-email`, which drains the lab-devel inbox one
message at a time without a model deciding when to stop. Each pass:

- runs `just get-up-to-date`, which fetches every remote, rebases
  unmerged trunk work and the mail outbox, and runs notmuch new;
- takes the oldest inbox message from `just get-oldest-inbox-message`;
- runs a fresh `claude --permission-mode auto -p "/process-email <id>"`
  with its output sent to /dev/null;
- checks with notmuch that the message left the inbox, and posts to
  the operator's ntfy topic with `just notify`.

The loop ends when the inbox is empty. If a pass leaves its message in
the inbox, it notifies "stuck: <subject>" and exits 1, rather than
running claude on that message forever. This replaces the loop that
reran claude until the model touched tmp/done.

The ntfy topic URL is a secret, so it lives on the host in
/jails/data/lab-claude/secrets/notify-url, mounted read-only at
/data/secrets the way lab-mail's credentials are. NOTIFY_URL in the
environment overrides it. With neither set, the loop runs and sends
nothing. A post that fails or takes longer than ten seconds only
warns, so it cannot stop the inbox from draining.

/process-email takes an optional id argument and falls back to `just
get-oldest-inbox-message`, so running the skill by hand still works.
Its step 1 runs the same `just get-up-to-date`, leaving the model only
what needs judgement: conflicted commits and patches applied with
edits.

Testing: with a stub `claude` on PATH that answers nothing and
NOTIFY_URL pointing at a local listener, the loop fetched, picked the
oldest message, posted "stuck: <subject>" with a "Title:
process-email" header, and exited 1. When the listener never
answered, notify gave up after ten seconds with a warning and exited
0. With no topic configured, notify exits 0 and posts nothing.

Setup on beastie, before restarting lab-claude:

    mkdir -p /jails/data/lab-claude/secrets
    cd /jails/data/lab-claude/secrets
    printf '%s\n' 'https://ntfy.sh/<topic>' > notify-url
    chown -R 0:15000 .
    chmod 0750 .
    chmod 0640 notify-url

Note: "[PATCH] claude: Treat unintegrated mail as revisable drafts" [1]
and "[PATCH] claude: Update stale threads from process-email" [2] also
edit step 2 of the skill. Whichever lands second will need a small
rebase.

